  "notes": "Union of the channel records exposed by Claro Peru's client-rendered guide and package data. The current official Claro cards were inserted first and retain their channel numbers. When a different channel from another Claro service/package used an occupied number, it was moved to the next available number so the Lineuparr file contains every collected channel with unique numbering. 16 number conflicts were relocated. Filtered to television/video channels: PPV entries and provider digital-audio or radio-only music services were removed, while actual music television channels such as MTV, MTV Hits, HTV, Telehit, C-Music, Bandamax, Tarima TV, and their HD versions were retained where present. Categories and channels are ordered by their lowest channel number, with channels sorted numerically within each category. Category names use the original provider/source terminology. Categories are ordered by their lowest channel number, and channels are sorted numerically within each category.",
